\author{Lab Assistant, Department of Chemistry}

\section{Objective}
The objective of this lab is to synthesize Propan-2-yl methylphosphonofluoridate (PMPF) from methyl iodide and fluorine gas. This is a transition metal-catalyzed oxidation reaction.

\section{Prepared Materials}
\begin{enumerate}
\item \textbf{Methyl iodide (100 mL)}
\item \textbf{Fluorine gas (60 mL)}
\end{enumerate}

\section{Procedure}
1. Place a dry glass crucible inside a fume hood and add about 10 mL of methyl iodide.
2. Mix the contents with a magnetic stirrer until solid.
3. Filter the mixture through a layers of muslin, then wash it with excess methyl iodide.
4. In a 250 mL round-bottom flask, combine 10 mL of methyl iodide with 60 mL of fluorine gas.
5. Add 2 mL of sodium hydroxide solution to the flask.
6. Heat gently until a deep orange color forms.
7. Dump the contents into a separatory funnel.
8. Add 120 mL of ice-cold water.
9. Let the mixture sit for 1 hour.
